tags: event
face-image: img/spd.jpg

= The <span style="color: #E3000F;">**social democrats**</span> choose their path out of the crisis

Since the onset of the economic crisis, the <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span>, much to the frustration of its trade unions, has refused to endorse an economic plan, with Rudolf Hilferding commited to fiscal orthodoxy and against helping capitalism in its final stage. Yet the past two years, marked by poverty, hunger and violence, have pushed the bulk of the party against the Center leadership, and a congress will be held to determine their path forward. There are two main economic plans being discussed, the party's left proposes a nationalization plan, which would act not only to solve the crisis, but also prepare for a transition into a soviet republic. The trade unions and reformist factions have rallied behind the "WTB Plan," consisting of mass public works with deficit spending, if necessary.

- @nationalization_plan: The <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span> adopts the nationalization plan.
- @wtp_plan: Woytinsky and his supporters manage to sway the party.

@nationalization_plan
view-if: spd_left > spd_right
on-arrival: spd_left_plan = 1; workers_spd += 5; unemployed_spd += 5; socialism += 1; spd_relation -= 5;

With nationalizations being the preferred alternative for the center marxists, the party's left has come out on top of this congress, solidifying their <span style="color: #E3000F;">**socialist**</span> roots. [? if unemployed >= 10: They will begin implementing the plan as soon as possible, even if it requires deficit spending or seizing factories. ?]

@wtp_plan
view-if: spd_left <= spd_right
on-arrival: spd_wtb_plan = 1; workers_spd += 3; new_middle_spd += 2; old_middle_spd += 2; rural_spd += 2; unemployed_spd += 3;

With broad support within the ADGB, mass public works will now become the platform for the <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span>, broadening their appeal to all strata of society. [? if unemployed >= 10: They will begin implementing the plan as soon as possible, likely requiring deficit spending. ?]
